# tilesets.pdl - how the SAME world looks (BOOK 16.game/RPG-DUST-PETSLIKE-BOARD-DESIGN.md D5-D7). The world (map.txt) never changes with the tileset, only the art of the seven height bands does.
# TILESET | id | label | kind | root
#   kind: rmmv = RPG Maker tiles painted by the skin (root unused) | plain = flat colours | png = loose PNG files under #.NNEST_ASSETS/<root> | csv = palette sprite folders under &.widgits/palettes/sprites/<root>
# TILE | tileset | band | source | tint
#   band: deep water sand grass forest rock snow. source: png = path under the root (an animated strip uses its first frame; any size is box-averaged to 24 px); csv = the sprite folder number.
#   tint (optional, rrggbb): multiplies the picture (Mineclonia's grass and water textures are grey, the game colours them). forest, rock and snow are drawn over the grass tile; the others replace it.
# A band with no TILE row falls back to a flat colour, so a new tileset works with only the rows it has. The choice is a TILESET row in state/look_ledger.txt (append-only), not a file edit.
TILESET | rmmv  | RPG Maker       | rmmv  | -
TILESET | plain | Plain colours   | plain | -
TILESET | cdda  | Cataclysm DDA   | png   | cdda-tilesets/gfx/UltimateCataclysm
TILESET | mcl   | Mineclonia      | png   | mineclonia/mods/ITEMS/mcl_core/textures
TILESET | doom  | Doom (Freedoom) | csv   | doom/flats
